<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n58151" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κνημ-ός</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>projecting limb, shoulder</i> of
			a mountain (above the foot, <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				1498.42
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> (always in pl.), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἴδης κνημοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					2.821
				</span></i>
			, al., cf. <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				4.337
			</span></i>: sg., <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Ap.</u>
				283
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Orph.
				<u>A.</u>
				465
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δημόσιος κ.</span> public <i>grove</i>,
			prob. in <i><span class="en">
				<u>TAM</u>
				2(1).64
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Telmessus</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> Arg., 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρίγανος</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				265.40
			</span></i>.</div>
